<h2>Greetings, I'm Roman!</h2>
<p> 
    Welcome to my website. While my primary interest is programming, this site contains information from
    a wide range of fields that I find interesting including engineering, mathematics, and psychology.
    I am currently working on building a better understanding of physics and electronics to better
    understand the inner workings of computers!
</p>

<img src="/assets/images/personal/bridge.jpg" alt="Photo of Me">

<h2>Studies</h2>
<p>
    I will be starting college this upcoming fall, so most of my programming knowledge has come from building projects and looking at documentation.
    Some resources I found helpful were <a href="https://www.udemy.com/user/stephen-ulibarri-3/" target="_blank">Stephen Ulibarri's courses</a> for learning
    Unreal and <a href="https://cs50.harvard.edu/web/" target="_blank">Harvard's CS50w</a> for learning the basics of web development.
    Some courses are good for starting out, but I think the fastest way to learn is just to go out and build something, struggle,
    fail, make mistakes, but come out a better programmer in the end.
</p>

